If the first character of a signed conversion is not a sign or if a signed conversion results in no characters, a &lt;space&gt;
shall be prefixed to the result. This means that if the &lt;space&gt; and [CODE164] flags both appear, the &lt;space&gt; flag
shall be ignored.

The next call prints out the group name if it is found using [A535][I536]getgrgid[/I536]()[/A535];
[A537][I538]getgrgid[/I538]()[/A537] is very similar to [A539][I540]getpwuid[/I540]()[/A539] except that it shall return group information based on the group number. Once
again, if the group is not found, the program prints the numeric value of the group for the entry.

The following example uses [A573][I574]strfmon[/I574]()[/A573] to convert a number and store it as a
formatted monetary string named [I575]convbuf[/I575]. If the first number is printed, the program prints the format and the description;
otherwise, it just prints the number.
